NAME
    results - query recorded trials, unit timings, and flakes

SYNOPSIS
    results [--last N]
    results --slowest N [--tier T] [--since D]
    results --flaky [--since D]
    results --misses [--since D]
    results --quarantine
    results --selected TRIAL
    results unit UNIT
    results test NAME
    results export [--since D]

DESCRIPTION
    Read-only query command of the emusen.testing module. Reads the
    SQLite testing store at ~/.local/share/EmuSen/testing/studio.db
    (or the path named by EMUSEN_TESTING_DB).

    With no flags or subcommands, prints the most recent trials (number,
    start time, verdict, tier, tree, branch, duration, and backfill
    source if applicable).

    Subcommands:
        unit UNIT   History for UNIT, newest first.
        test NAME   History for test NAME, newest first.
        export      Emit every trial since --since as JSON Lines (one
                    JSON object per line).

OPTIONS
    --last N
        Number of recent trials to list (default: 10).
    --slowest N
        Show the N slowest units by median wall time, with run counts
        and maximum duration.
    --tier T
        Filter --slowest results to tier T.
    --since D
        Time window filter using a duration suffix such as 14d, 12h, or
        30m.
    --flaky
        List tests recorded as flaky (with runners) and tests with
        conflicting outcomes under the same input key.
    --misses
        List impact(1) selection misses recorded by nightly runs.
    --quarantine
        List active test quarantines.
    --selected TRIAL
        Show why each unit was selected in trial number TRIAL (reason,
        triggering file, key, and source trial if reused).

ENVIRONMENT
    EMUSEN_TESTING_DB
        Override path to the studio SQLite database.

EXAMPLES
    results --slowest 15 --tier land
    results --flaky --since 14d
    results unit "cargo:EmuSen/Cores/Sony/Sapphire - PlayStation 2"
    results test Every_audited_window_state
    results export --since 30d > trials.jsonl

EXIT STATUS
    0   Query completed.
    2   Invalid subcommand, invalid option or duration, or store error.

SEE ALSO
    trial(1), ingest(1), impact(1), units(1)
